      "writtenOn": "2017-03-14T18:57:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "INTERNAL_ERROR \u003d\u003d\u003e Unexpected vendor internal error scenario while processing the request. Ex. SIM failure when trying read the SPN of the SIM card to form the response.\nMODEM_ERROR \u003d\u003d\u003e Invalid payload response (sanity correlation of items like length / validity )\nRADIO_NOT_AVAILABLE \u003d\u003d\u003e When modem didn\u0027t start\nOPERATION_NOT_ALLOWED \u003d\u003d\u003e Returned when device is in CDMA mode / Global mode\nABORTED \u003d\u003d\u003e When the manual scan is aborted due to high priority activity like voice call\nDEVICE_IN_USE \u003d\u003d\u003e Radio is already busy in high priority activity like voice call\nNO_MEMORY \u003d\u003d\u003e Not sufficient memory to process the request",
      "parentUuid": "12ed8273_ab3b2468",
      "revId": "50ed146b9126c43d5796f1357d13dccaddbff71c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "42ecd144_d42b253d",
        "filename": "radio/1.0/IRadioResponse.hal",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 796,
      "author": {
        "id": 1141163
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-14T19:01:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Those two sounds like the new \u0027generic errors\" to me.\nJack, To me it looks better that GENERIC_FAILURE, I think we still need to have these for cases that could not be mapped to the remaining 5. I just gave some examples in the last comment.",
      "parentUuid": "dcff6b8b_803eafa6",
      "revId": "50ed146b9126c43d5796f1357d13dccaddbff71c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
